From 201154cdb439220c759363868ee8d2d299ccc0d6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 10:53:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: generated code compatible with device code, numerical
 type of the generic interfaces

- code generated for the behaviours and the material properties usable
  in device code (device_compatible_class DSL option, static variables
  read through TFEL_STATIC_VARIABLE, @SharedData keyword, comparison to a
  numerical jacobian and profiling on the host only).
- real_type DSL option: double (default) or float for the generic and
  generic-parallel interfaces, symbol of the size of the numerical type,
  convergence criteria adapted to float, refused by the other interfaces
  and by MTest.
- generic interface: displacement gradient for the finite strain
  behaviours, axial component of the deformation gradient in plane
  stress, integration drivers usable in device code.
- graph of the conversions of the tangent operators: direct conversions
  (edges DTAU_DF -> DPK1_DF and DTAU_DDF -> DPK1_DF among others), so
  that any usual native tangent operator reaches the requested ones in one
  conversion; path chosen by a breadth first search, which returns the
  same paths as the enumeration of the maximal paths at a cost
  independent of their number; strain measure wrappers of the generic
  interface (Green-Lagrange, Hencky) calling the direct conversions.
- device code of the finite strain behaviours: the tangent operator (or
  the prediction operator) defined by the behaviour is computed by a
  single call in computeConsistentTangentOperator
  (computePredictionOperator), the functions of the operators deduced from
  it only converting it; the kernels of the GPUs, which inline every call,
  held one copy of the code of the behaviour per tangent operator handled.
  The code compiled for the host is unchanged.
- final conversion of the tangent operator computed in the storage of Dt
  (thelfer/tfel#1489).
- setUninitialized method of the local variables and of the integration
  variables, tensorial gradients left uninitialized by the constructors of
  the generic interface, numerical jacobian saved only if it must be
  restored (thelfer/tfel#1491).
- simultaneous_substitutions option of the Default and TDLS linear
  system solvers: partial inverse of the jacobian computed by a single
  substitution (thelfer/tfel#1493); rows of the blocks of the tensorial
  integration variables in computePartialJacobianInvert
  (thelfer/tfel#1495).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
